  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When using a different system locale than en_US the parsing of dates containing short weekdays may fail if the particular locale does not recognize the name of the weekday. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Given the date string: \"Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT\", the pattern \"EEE, dd MMMM yyyyy HH:mm:ss z\" and the system locale de_DE.UTF-8 (export LC_ALL=\"de_DE.UTF-8\"), the parser will throw an exception. The correct date string for this locale would be \"Do, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT\". The same may apply to month short names. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "The affected class is org.fcrepo.server.utilities.DateUtility. Also, when running the integration tests with configA the test testParseDate() in org.fcrepo.server.utilities.TestDateUtility fails.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The suggested fix is to use the en_US locale when initializing SimpleDateFormat.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
